  "method": "Independent model editorial review of all 1,599 candidate headwords and supplied English sense summaries, with full candidate records checked for ambiguous inflection, abbreviation, name and homograph cases. Explicit decisions below cover each candidate exactly once. This is not native-human certification or a claim that every dictionary sense was independently verified. Nineteen additional Ё candidates were then individually reviewed against all supplied eligible senses after the frequency-only Е fallback was introduced.",
  "policy": "Retain ordinary contemporary Russian standalone words, including independent function words, predicatives, lexicalized plurals and ordinary substantivized readings. Exclude inflection-only records, abbreviations, misspellings, name-only or specialized homographs with misleading spelling frequency, and prominent insult ambiguities. Ё/Е and Й/И stay distinct. A source-labelled independent sense is necessary but not sufficient.",
  "retainedDistinctions": {
    "ВСЕ / ВСЁ": "Both retained: everyone and everything are independent pronoun readings, not aliases.",
    "БЕРЕТ / БЕРЁТ": "БЕРЕТ retained for the standalone beret noun; it is not an alias for the finite verb БЕРЁТ.",
    "ЧАСЫ / ОЧКИ / ДЕНЬГИ / ВОРОТА": "Ordinary lexicalized plural nouns retained; this is not blanket admission of plural inflections.",
    "ДОЛЖЕН / РАД": "Independent predicative headwords retained, not inferred solely from adjectival form spelling.",
    "ПИСАТЬ": "Ordinary write sense qualifies; other dictionary senses do not remove the independent neutral headword.",
    "НЁБО / НЕБО": "Both retained: palate and sky are ordinary distinct nouns; fallback frequency alone was not treated as proof.",
    "ПЕРЁД / ПЕРЕД": "Both retained for independent front noun and before/in-front-of preposition readings, with spelling-frequency ambiguity acknowledged.",
    "Ё fallback": "Actor, volume, reception, report, clearly, forward, moreover, black, concerning, child, airplane and youth readings are ordinary independent words. No Е gameplay aliases were introduced."
